# The sea floor (Emerald's MUS_UNDERWATER role, plan 21 · H5): slow and weightless, a flute drifting over a
# vibraphone's rippling arpeggios in E major, a pad that swells like light through the water and a deep bass far
# below. The same by day and night, as the sea floor's light is. Original composition for this game.
title Under the Sea
tempo 72
meter 4/4
reverb 0.55
night none

track lead flute vol=0.6 pan=0.05 rev=0.56
  L o5 b2 g+4 f+4 | o5 g+2. e4 | o5 c+2 e4 g+4 | o5 f+2. r4 |
  o5 b2 o6 c+4 d+4 | o6 d+2 o5 b4 g+4 | o5 a2 g+4 e4 | o5 f+2. r4 |

track ripple vibraphone vol=0.3 pan=-0.3 rev=0.5
  L o4 e8 g+8 b8 o5 d+8 o4 b8 g+8 e8 g+8 | o4 c+8 e8 g+8 b8 g+8 e8 c+8 e8 | o4 a8 o5 c+8 e8 g+8 e8 c+8 o4 a8 o5 c+8 | o4 b8 o5 d+8 f+8 a8 f+8 d+8 o4 b8 o5 d+8 |
  o4 e8 g+8 b8 o5 d+8 o4 b8 g+8 e8 g+8 | o4 g+8 b8 o5 d+8 f+8 d+8 o4 b8 g+8 b8 | o4 a8 o5 c+8 e8 g+8 e8 c+8 o4 a8 o5 c+8 | o4 b8 o5 e8 f+8 a8 f+8 e8 o4 b8 o5 e8 |

track swell pad vol=0.26 pan=0.25 rev=0.62
  L o4 (e g+ b)1 | (c+ e g+)1 | (c+ e a)1 | (d+ f+ b)1 |
  (e g+ b)1 | (d+ g+ b)1 | (c+ e a)1 | (e f+ b)1 |

track bass contrabass vol=0.6 rev=0.3
  L o2 e1 | o2 c+1 | o1 a1 | o1 b1 |
  o2 e1 | o2 g+1 | o1 a1 | o1 b1 |
